From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:38:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 5317: the contact enrichment queue lives in the database and
 survives a restart

The queue of saved contacts waiting for their score and enrichment lived in
this process's memory, so every deploy dropped what was waiting (the tester's
launch report F10; Misho's yes to Q7). Migration 242 adds enrichment_jobs;
each saved contact is a row, four workers claim the oldest with SKIP LOCKED,
a failed job is marked failed and never stops the queue, and on start a job a
restart cut off mid-run is queued again. The daily per-owner share decides,
at queue time, whether a job enriches or only scores.

